Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["InfraMidpoint", "ObjectName",
 CellID->1224892054,ExpressionUUID->"8393d601-4014-44ba-afc9-60862df940ec"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->"723a6d71-b0b2-4932-aac8-5de2c0f23331"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["InfraMidpoint"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraMidpoint", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["p", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["q", "TI"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "aff3df88-65c6-4a8c-b415-d7f21803aa97"],
 "\[LineSeparator]",
 "is the exact midpoint point family between ",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["q", "TI"],
 ".",
 "\n"
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"c7d88a03-e11b-46bf-ac8f-a4cd13548b4a"],

Cell["\<\
The graph must be finite, simple, undirected and unweighted, with valid \
vertex anchors. Unsupported arguments and properties stay unevaluated. The \
head is inert until a graph-aware reader or named sampler evaluates it.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"4c1a255a-820c-4e8c-801c-532b78629c13"],

Cell["\<\
One representative is one raw vertex label, including a List-valued label. \
The complete family has distinct vertices in graph vertex order and unit \
vertex density. Supported measurements are \"VertexDensity\", \
\"Cardinality\", \"CountingMeasure\", \"Subgraph\" and \"RiemannianMeasure\". \
The last measure uses the existing interior-support law. \"Graph\", \
\"EdgeDensity\", \"Length\", \"Area\" and \"Volume\" are unsupported for \
these point families.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"bb239660-b87a-43dc-ac15-b803aff764f1"],

Cell["\<\
A vertex belongs exactly when both endpoint distances equal half the finite \
endpoint distance. Odd distance and disconnected endpoints give an empty \
family; equal anchors give one point. This differs from the segment \
\"Midpoint\" measurement, which retains middle-layer construction density and \
can contain two layers.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"ee86dde5-4269-48c9-a5f9-52732acc11b9"]
}, Open  ]],

